{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su2","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L119-L121","doc":"`SU(2)`, spin alone: `S = −(3/4)·C(n,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su3","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L113-L117","doc":"`SU(3)` — **the eightfold way's own flavour group** — falls to the same\nidentity: `S = −(4/6)·C(n,2) = −(2/3)·C(n,2)`. The eightfold way cannot supply a\nthree-body cumulant either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_su4","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L108-L111","doc":"`SU(4)`, recovering the merged `SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount` result:\n`4·4·S = −5·2·C(n,2)`, i.e. `S = −(5/8)·C(n,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_add_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_add_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L101-L106","doc":"Proportionality in the form that shows no `n`-dependence survives for a\ncoordination weight to inherit: the two-body sum plus `(N+1)` times the pair\ncount vanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**The two-body sum is exactly proportional to the pair count, for every `N`.**\n`2N·S(n) = −(N+1)·C(n,2)`, stated here as `4N·S = −(N+1)·2C(n,2)`.\n\nThis is the load-bearing statement: such an interaction contributes a constant\nper pair, hence a constant coordination weight, hence `b₃ = 0`. No\nantisymmetric-column Casimir of any `SU(N)` can carry three-body content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimir_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimir_affine","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L84-L88","doc":"**The Casimir is affine in the pair count, for every `N`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSumX4N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairSumX4N","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L80-L82","doc":"`4N · S(n)` where `S(n) = ½(C₂([1^n]) − n·C₂(fund))` is the sum a two-body\n`SU(N)`-invariant interaction contributes over the antisymmetric `n`-body state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairCountX2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.pairCountX2","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L77-L78","doc":"`2 · C(n,2) = n(n−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimirFundX2N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimirFundX2N","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L74-L75","doc":"`2N · C₂(fund) = N² − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimirAntisymX2N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.casimirAntisymX2N","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AntisymmetricCasimirIsTwoBody.lean#L70-L72","doc":"`2N · C₂([1^n])` for the fully antisymmetric representation of `SU(N)`,\nwhose Casimir is `(N+1)n(N−n)/(2N)`. Scaled to stay in a ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}